        "Location": "With Selarial",
        "Name": "Acid Fang",
        "Notes": "FORMERLY: Nightwind (renamed after enhancement)<br><br>PHYSICAL: Slightly curved bastard sword with acid-etched runes that shift like liquid. Crossguard incorporates black dragon scales. Pommel contains reservoir of refined dragon acid (green-black liquid pulsing with wielder's heartbeat).<br><br>BASE PROPERTIES:<br>• +3 magical weapon with finesse property<br>• 3d6 acid damage on hit (bonus action toggle)<br>• Critical hits cause ongoing acid damage (2d6) for 1d4 rounds<br><br>SOUL-ENHANCED ABILITIES:<br>• Improved Spiritual Pressure: 15ft radius oppressive force, DC 17 WIS or disadvantage<br>• Shadow Manipulation: Shape darkness into semi-solid constructs (tentacles, barriers, platforms, tunnels), up to 30ft cube, 3 constructs, allies see through<br>• Acid Mist: 20ft radius acid cloud (1/short rest), 2d6 acid damage, disadvantage on perception<br>• Corrosive Strike: 3/day, bypasses acid resistance, reduces target AC by 2<br>• Dimensional Acid: Strikes ethereal/incorporeal/phase-shifted enemies<br><br>ORIGINAL NIGHTWIND PROPERTIES (Preserved):<br>• Bloodthirsty aura<br>• Underworld darkness manipulation (now enhanced)<br>• 10% lightning strike chance<br><br>ORIGIN: Created Session 5 through ritual with Selarial as 'Nightwind.' Enhanced by Helvraen using black dragon (Maladrax) materials and draconic essence.<br><br>EVOLUTION POTENTIAL: Enhanced shadow constructs, acid pool creation dissolving planar boundaries, shadow step teleportation.<br><br>NOTE: Attunement requires connection to Dodecahedron. Responds to Selarial's intent, anticipating needs.",
        "Origin": "Maladrax dragon materials + Session 5 ritual evolution",
